create GDG BASE:
We use the IBM utility IDCAMS with the DEFINE GENERATIONDATAGROUP command.

//GDGCR JOB (ACCT),'CREATE GDG'
//STEP01 EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  DEFINE GDG -
    (NAME(USER1.INPUT.GDG) -
     LIMIT(5) -
     SCRATCH -
     NOEMPTY)
/*
Explanation of parameters:
Parameter	Explanation
NAME	Name of the GDG BASE
LIMIT(5)	Maintains a maximum of 5 generations
SCRATCH	Deletes the physical dataset when rolled off
NOSCRATCH	Keeps the physical dataset when rolled off
EMPTY	When the limit is reached, removes all existing generations
NOEMPTY	When the limit is reached, removes only the oldest generation

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to create GDG generations
//STEP02 EXEC PGM=IEFBR14
//GDGFILE DD DSN=USER1.INPUT.GDG(+1),
//           DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//           SPACE=(TRK,(5,5)),
//           DCB=(RECFM=FB,LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=800)



Remember these four combinations:
          Parameters	Behaviour
````````SCRATCH,EMPTY	Deletes all generations when limit is reached
````````SCRATCH,NOEMPTY	Deletes only the oldest generation
````````NOSCRATCH,EMPTY	Uncatalogs all generations
````````NOSCRATCH,NOEMPTY	Uncatalogs only the oldest generation

"GDG is used to maintain multiple versions of datasets. We create a GDG BASE using IDCAMS DEFINE GDG and specify parameters like LIMIT, SCRATCH, NOSCRATCH, EMPTY and NOEMPTY. We use (+1) to create a new generation, (0) for the current generation and (-1) for the previous generation."



